      "Dead ball is 41-52% of each match (tracking BallStatus).",
      "6.5-11 possession spells per live minute (BAR-ATH public: 4.2 from 17 spells).",
      "The DFL ball is frozen with exactly zero speed in every dead frame, an artifact absent from BAR-ATH; ball clues trained on it learn a shortcut."
    ]
  },
  "takeaways": [
    "V14 beats V13 on the bench at every level (+0.006 to +0.018) and scores 0.554 publicly; retrained with player drop-out it is best in the most realistic condition (0.498).",
    "Missing players cost every method about 0.035 but keep the lead over V7 and the baseline.",
    "V15 and the crowd rule are rejected on answer-free and bench evidence despite a higher public score for V15."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Bench labels for Metrica are event-derived; DFL labels count possession changes more often than BAR-ATH appears to.",
    "Player drop-out picks random players; real drop-outs may favour players far from the action.",
    "Public scores reuse 17 inspected spells."
  ]
